<!--
  The compat flavour, defined by what it does not declare.

  No <permission> and no <provider>. That is the whole difference from `host`,
  and it is deliberately expressed as an empty manifest rather than as a removal
  in the build script, so that the diff between the two variants is one file you
  can read.

  What it costs: third-party car apps will refuse Headway as a host, because
  HostValidator's only reachable branch is "the caller holds
  android.car.permission.TEMPLATE_RENDERER" and a permission cannot be held
  unless something defines it. The Car apps tab will bind, be refused by name,
  and say so. Car apps also lose the way they ask whether they are being
  projected, so some decline to start their car service at all.

  What it does not cost: everything else. The car link, video, touch, audio,
  voice, the dashboard, maps, phone, messages and media all work identically —
  they were never downstream of these two names, and taking the whole app down
  with them is the bug this flavour exists to fix.

  A locally built debug APK of a car app still works against this flavour:
  both OsmAnd and Organic Maps branch on FLAG_DEBUGGABLE to
  ALLOW_ALL_HOSTS_VALIDATOR, which consults no permission.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" />
